    "result_text": "Claims now get their number when they're settled or approved, not when they're opened. All four tests in the spec pass under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What changed** (all in `ClaimService.java`):\n- **Opening a claim** no longer gives it a number. That includes claims that go to REVIEW and claims a steward later reviews to OPEN, so OPEN, PENDING and REVIEW claims show no number.\n- **Settling a claim** gives it the next number in its sequence (sheet-wide per fiscal year, or per period), placed by its due-by date. A clerk's settle that goes to PENDING gets no number; the number comes when a steward approves it. In the audit file, `CLAIM_SETTLED` and `CLAIM_APPROVED` now carry `number=\u2026` before `due=\u2026`.\n- **Splitting a claim** creates the new claim with no number, and the audit line ends `into=` with nothing after it.\n- **Moving a claim** to another person: since OPEN and PENDING claims have no number now, there's normally nothing to renumber. A claim numbered under the old rule is still renumbered on a move, as before.\n- **Re-dating** has no number to keep. **Voiding** still keeps a settled claim's number.\n- **Existing numbers** are left alone, so the stored data needs no migration. A claim that already has a number keeps it when it's settled.\n\n**One change outside the request.** Scenario 2 kept failing on a claim that was refused for falling in a closed period. That came from how payment terms are worked out, not from numbering. When a claim is added, the person's grade used to choose its terms was taken as of the sheet's today; it's now taken as of the claim's date. In the test, Cam's claim is dated 2026-03-01, when Cam was grade A, so it gets A's 20 days and is due by 2026-03-30, which the test expects. Using today's grade (C, 30 days) pushed it into the closed April period. The terms values themselves are still the ones in force on the sheet's today, and splitting a claim works as before. This is a separate change in behaviour, so look it over before keeping it.\n\nI also updated a few comments that said a claim is numbered \"when opened\", in `SettingsService.java`, `Sheet.java`, `settings.ts` and `settings.service.ts`. I made those after the last test run, but they're comment-only.",
